    "items": [
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/185269030?u=1fc22565ccf4566b6f734fabaa87e03d9a31cfe4&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Adds a note to the <code class=\"notranslate\">IdleDeadline.timeRemaining()</code> documentation clarifying that the returned value is an estimate of available idle time and should not be treated as a fixed countdown.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The current documentation may imply that <code class=\"notranslate\">timeRemaining()</code> continuously counts down during an idle period. However, the browser's estimate can change and may suddenly drop to <code class=\"notranslate\">0</code> when higher-priority (latency-critical) work arrives. This update helps readers better understand the behavior of the API and avoid incorrect assumptions when scheduling background tasks.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The note was added to the introduction section of the page and is based on the discussion in the linked issue regarding how browsers determine remaining idle time.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #37250.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"2746262413\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/37250\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/37250/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/37250\">#37250</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/44373",
            "title": "Clarify that timeRemaining() is an estimate and not a fixed countdown (#37250)",
            "date_modified": "2026-06-07T17:12:35.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-06-07T17:12:18.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "BHUVANSH855",
                "url": "https://github.com/BHUVANSH855"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7352080?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Addresses the dev-docs-needed requirements of <a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2044712\" rel=\"nofollow\">Bug 2044712</a> \"Expose colors and icons to extensions\" including:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>a release note</li>\n<li>methods 'getSupportedColors()' and <code class=\"notranslate\">getSupportedIcons()</code></li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">BCD is provided in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"4607945053\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/29814\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29814/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29814\">mdn/browser-compat-data#29814</a>.</p>",
